10263:       trigger: "exp-05 is the only contrast in this batch that cleared a paired test: averaging two same-init checkpoints whose dev-300 errors overlapped in 47 of 74 items bought +4.4 pts at n=500 (McNemar p = 0.0198). The soup has exactly two ingredients and they were NOT built to be diverse - exp-04 reused exp-02's corpus verbatim plus RFT rows. A third ingredient trained to be deliberately decorrelated is the same lever again, and it is the only lever the remaining 3.9 h affords."
10264:       trigger_evidence:
10265:         - {path: /home/ben/task/analysis/exp-05_summary.json, locator: "soup 0.736 vs 0.692 / 0.688 at n=500", observation: "the averaging gain, measured under one protocol in one session"}
10266:         - {path: /home/ben/task/memory/cards/exp-05.yaml, locator: "result.diagnostic_result: 52 fixed / 30 regressed over 82 discordant pairs", observation: "the two-ingredient average is already recovering a large net item swing; error decorrelation is the active ingredient"}
10267:         - {path: /home/ben/task/memory/cards/exp-04.yaml, locator: "conclusion.verdict contradicted, decision reject", observation: "an ingredient does not need to be a good checkpoint on its own - exp-04 was a null as a model and still carried the soup"}
10268:       alternatives_rejected:
10269:         - {option: "Stop here and ship the verified two-way soup", reason: "this is the fallback and it stays live throughout - final_model/ already holds the greedy soup, CPU-load-checked and re-scored from a fresh process at 0.7467 (n=150). exp-06 only replaces it if the three-way beats it at n=500, so the downside is spent time, not a worse submission."}
10270:         - {option: "Souping in exp-02/epoch1 or exp-04/epoch1 as the third ingredient (free, no training)", reason: "both are much weaker (dev-300 0.6933 and 0.7067 vs 0.7533/0.7700) and a uniform average is dragged by a weak member; the cheap version of this idea is available but the evidence says it would subtract"}
10271:         - {option: "A second RFT round, or GRPO, from the soup", reason: "exp-04 already showed the RFT line is null here, and 3.9 h with an unclosed card is the wrong place to bring up a new trainer"}
10272:         - {option: "Same corpus, different seed only", reason: "seed alone changes data order and init noise but leaves the 74k targets identical; changing the OpenMathInstruct-2 slice (13652 problems new), the few-shot fraction (0.08 -> 0.12) and the learning rate (1.5e-5 -> 1.0e-5) buys decorrelation along four axes at the same cost"}
10273:         - {option: "Three epochs, or a larger corpus, to make ingredient C stronger than its predecessors", reason: "C does not need to be the best model, it needs to be a good model that fails differently; 2 epochs is the recipe already calibrated on this hardware (~1.55 h) and the budget has no room for more"}
